# Olife conventions

You are building and operating **olife1.com** (Olife). Product owner is human; agents execute within these rules.

## Phase gate

- Until the owner replies **`APPROVE BUILD`**, do not write or merge product/application code that changes runtime behavior.
- Phase 1 docs live on branch `phase-1-plan` — do not merge to `main` without owner approval.
- **`APPROVE DEPLOY`** is required for production. Staging deploy may be autonomous only after APPROVE BUILD.

## Stack (locked)

- Django + Django templates only. **No** Next.js, React, or separate SPA.
- Supabase Postgres via `DATABASE_URL`. No Railway Postgres for app data unless owner approves a documented blocker.
- Media: Supabase Storage.
- Hosting: Railway (`web` + `worker`; staging + prod).
- Multi-agent: LangGraph **library** self-hosted — **not** LangGraph Platform.
- LLM: Gemini Flash default; Pro opt-in; thin adapter for Anthropic/OpenAI fallback.
- Monorepo: Django app + `/agents` + `/chatbot` (Telegram + `/admin/commands/` — no Google Chat).
- Control plane: plain text commands only; one router, two transports.

## Brand voice

- Read and obey `docs/BRAND.md`.
- Raw, reflective, grounded, honest, conversational — one person late at night.
- Never: guru, hustle-bro, corporate marketer, preachy textbook.

## Naming

- Agents: Orchestrator, Architect, Designer, FrontendBuilder, BackendBuilder, ContentMigrator, SEOSpecialist, CRMBuilder, Deployer, QAInspector, BrandVoice, SiteAuditor.
- Custom CRM at `/admin` (staff). Django admin at `/django-admin/`.
- Canonical host: `https://olife1.com`. www → apex 301.
- Fragments stay a first-class section named Fragments.

## Git / deploy

- `main` = production (auto-deploy). `staging` = staging.
- Feature branches → PR → `staging` → smoke → `main`.
- Every deploy, rollback, schema change, or destructive action: append `logs/audit/YYYY-MM-DD.md`.
- Every service exposes `GET /healthz`. Prefer Railway auto-rollback on failed healthcheck.
- Commit only `.env.example`. Never commit real keys, service accounts, or project IDs in docs — use placeholders like `<SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF>`.

## Product defaults

- Comments: registered-only; moderation queue in admin (flagged first).
- Newsletter: DB-only v1; `Subscriber.sync_*` fields for future providers.
- Google login: allauth plumbing OK; feature flag **OFF** at launch.
- Store: stub linking to `STORE_URL`. Podcast/Video: embeds only.
- English only for v1.
- Design: dark theme per `docs/DESIGN.md`; subtle motion only.

